  "prefLabel": "Gen 406.04 Facility-Based Genetic Counseling In-Service Training",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Gen 406.04 Facility-Based Genetic Counseling In-Service Training.\n\n(a) The licensee shall receive continuing education credit for participation in, or attendance at, a facility-based genetic counseling in-service training when the topic of the training is:\n\n(1) In the field of genetic counseling; or\n\n(2) Related to any psychological or physical condition for which genetic counseling is often or usually recommended.\n\n(b) The licensee shall receive one hour of continuing professional education credit for each clock hour of participation or attendance, to a maximum of 8 hours per renewal cycle.\n\n(c) Documentation of participation in, or attendance at, a facility-based genetic counseling in-service training shall be a photocopy of a memo from the genetic counselor’s supervisor of the facility stating:\n\n(1) The licensee’s name;\n\n(2) The name of the facility and the topic of the in-service training;\n\n(3) The date of the in-service training; and\n\n(4) The licensee’s hours of attendance.\n\nSource. #10687, eff 10-7-14; ss by #13556, eff 4-11-23 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Gen 400); ss by #14338, eff 10-7-25, EXPIRES: 10-7-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/gen400.html"
